* "KLD DC30 Ver C" (a 30 W Class A head of the Matchless DC30 kind, 4 EL84), transcribed from the supplied schematic (A4, 9-May-2019, from an image: some
* connections were hard to read and are noted below). Channel 1: V1a and V1b (two ECC83 triodes in parallel, 68k stopper, 220k plate), the CH1 VOLUME VR1 (A1M, with the
* 180p bright cap C40), V2b (1k5 / 22u, 100k) and the V2a cathode follower (56k), then the Top Boost network (R45 100k, C43 47p, C41 / C42 22n, R44 10k, TREBLE VR3 and
* BASS VR2, each A1M) and R6 220k. Channel 2: an EF86 (330k plate, 2k2 / 22u cathode), the six-position TONE switch SW4 (the coupling capacitor C6 to C11) with C12
* 180p always in, CH2 VOLUME VR4 (A1M, 180p bright cap C44, 470k load R46). The selected channel feeds the phase inverter (poweramp.net), where MASTER and CUT are.
* The preamp is split in two netlists so a channel that is not heard is not solved: this one is channel 1 up to the V2a follower (solved for the jacks Channel 1
* and Both); stage_out.net has its own copy of the guitar input, channel 2 (always solved: 2 ports), channel 1's Top Boost network driven from kf, and the outputs.
*
* Assumptions where the schematic is silent or ambiguous (change them here, not in code):
*  - the EF86 is not among the engine's tube models: an ECC83 triode stands in for it (the 1M screen resistor R70 and C70 are not modelled);
*  - the TONE switch: five of its six positions (the engine allows 2 to 5): the capacitors C11 10n, C10 4n7, C9 2n2, C8 1n and C6 360p (positions 1 to 5, the fullest first; C7 560p is left out); the
*    5M1 resistors give every capacitor's far end a DC return; C12 is always connected;
*  - C3 is 470 pF (the drawing writes small values in pF and larger ones as codes such as 473 or 104): channel 1 loses its lows before the volume pot;
*  - the two channels reach the phase inverter's two grids through the FX loops (bypassed) and 0.1u couplings; here the selected one drives the power amp's input; MASTER and CUT
*    are in the power amp netlist (the MASTER mixes the two phases after the inverter);
*  - the HT feeds: R30 22k / C30 22u (V1), R31 4k7 / C31 47u (V2) and R32 22k / C32 22u (EF86) from the rail x (HT2 after R34 2k2).

V VRAIL x 100 340
I VIN gin 1
R RSRC gin in 7k
* The guitar behind its source impedance (see the other amps): RSRC is the plain 7k source.
R RPU1 gin pkb1 1e12
.xfmr LPU1 L=2.5
  W pkb1 in 1 pu
.end
R RPU2 gin pkb2 1e12
.xfmr LPU2 L=5
  W pkb2 in 1 pu
.end
C CPU gin in 110p
R RPL gin in 1e12
R SWK1 in pkk1 1e12
C CCAB1 pkk1 0 200p
R SWK2 in pkk2 1e12
C CCAB2 pkk2 0 400p
R SWK4 in pkk4 1e12
C CCAB4 pkk4 0 800p


* HT feeds.
R R30 x n1 22k
C C30 n1 0 22u
R R31 x n2 4k7
C C31 n2 0 47u

* Jacks: SW_C1 / SW_C2 select the channel (closed 1 ohm / open 1e12), set by the jack modes. Channel 2's input (R42 1M, R43 68k and the input capacitance of its
* tube, about 170 pF) is repeated here as a load: the guitar sees both channels, as in one netlist.
R SW_C1 in j1 1
R R40 j1 0 1M
R R41 j1 g1 68k
R SW_C2 in j2 1e12
R R42 j2 0 1M
R R43 j2 ged 68k
C CMIL2 ged 0 170p

* Channel 1. V1a and V1b are two triodes in parallel (same nodes: one triode at scale 2): 220k plate, 1k5 with 0.1u and 22u on the cathode.
T V1 g1 p1 k1 12AX7 2
R R2 n1 p1 220k
R R1 k1 0 1k5
C C1 k1 0 0.1u
C C2 k1 0 22u

* CH1 VOLUME VR1 (A1M, wiper = output) with the 180p bright cap C40; C3 coupling.
C C3 p1 vt 470p
R VR1_T vt wv 1
R VR1_B wv 0 1
C C40 vt wv 180p

* V2b (100k plate, 1k5 / 22u) and the V2a cathode follower (grid on V2b's plate, 56k).
T V2B wv p2 k2 12AX7
R R47 n2 p2 100k
R R3 k2 0 1k5
C C4 k2 0 22u
T V2A p2 n2 kf 12AX7
R R4 kf 0 56k

* The load of the follower: channel 1's Top Boost network, R6 and the output switch repeated here (the stage after the cut at kf has the real ones; the knobs
* set both copies).
* Top Boost network: R45 100k and C43 47p from the follower, C41 / C42 22n, R44 10k to ground, BASS VR2 (top tb, wiper tc) and TREBLE VR3 (top tr, wiper wt, bottom tb).
R R45 kf ta 100k
C C43 kf tr 47p
C C41 ta tb 22n
C C42 ta tc 22n
R R44 tc 0 10k
R VR_KT tb tc 1
R VR_KB tc 0 1
R VR_TT tr wt 1
R VR_TB wt tb 1
R R6 wt o1 220k
R SW_O1 o1 md 1
R RM md 0 10M
